================
PAgP Security

Why we did this
================
EtherChannel can be formed using:

- LACP (IEEE Standard)
- PAgP (Cisco Proprietary)

PAgP (Port Aggregation Protocol) allows Cisco switches to dynamically negotiate and form an EtherChannel.

If PAgP is not properly controlled:

- Unauthorized links may join the bundle
- Misconfigured interfaces may cause instability
- Traffic may be forwarded incorrectly
- STP recalculations may occur

Administrators needed a secure method to ensure only valid interfaces participate in PAgP EtherChannels.

What will happen
================
1. PAgP packets are exchanged between Cisco devices.
2. Interfaces verify compatibility.
3. Matching interfaces join the EtherChannel.
4. Mismatched interfaces are rejected.
5. Stable bundle formation occurs.
6. Traffic forwarding remains consistent.

