Advantages and Disadvantages of this, hence what came next
==========================================================

Advantages
----------
1. Automatic EtherChannel negotiation.
2. Detects configuration mismatches.
3. Improves redundancy.
4. Simplifies EtherChannel deployment.
5. Prevents accidental member additions.
6. Cisco proprietary optimization.
7. Improves link reliability.

Disadvantages
-------------
1. Cisco proprietary protocol.
2. Not supported on non-Cisco devices.
3. Additional protocol overhead.
4. Less flexible than standard-based LACP.
5. Does not prevent broadcast storms.

Hence what came next
--------------------
Even with secure EtherChannels, excessive traffic can still overwhelm a network.

Examples:

- Broadcast Storms
- Multicast Flooding
- Unknown Unicast Flooding

Administrators needed traffic limiting mechanisms.

This led to:

Storm Control

which limits excessive Layer 2 traffic before it impacts the network.

One-Shot Configuration
======================

Configure PAgP

Switch(config)# interface range g0/1-2
Switch(config-if-range)# channel-group 1 mode desirable


Configure Secure Port-Channel

Switch(config)# interface port-channel1
Switch(config-if)# switchport mode trunk
Switch(config-if)# switchport trunk allowed vlan 10,20,30
Switch(config-if)# switchport trunk native vlan 999
Switch(config-if)# switchport nonegotiate


(Optional)

Switch(config)# interface port-channel1
Switch(config-if)# spanning-tree guard root


(Optional)

Switch(config)# interface range g0/1-2
Switch(config-if-range)# udld port aggressive

